  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.0 - BREAKING. Cancelling an upload now actually aborts the transfer instead of only greying out the UI. The progress bar reports real progress, and a server-processing phase is shown once the bytes have landed. Duplicates are reported as Skipped rather than as errors. New: GetUploadHeadersAsync and SendCredentials, so the file transfer can carry the user's identity. Breaking: IFileUploadClientService methods take FileProcessingOptions, and GetPolicyTokenAsync is replaced by GetEffectiveLimitsAsync - limits are now fetched from the server rather than declared twice; FileProcessingOptions.EnabledFeatures is replaced by the VerifyLocalDuplicates flag; MaxConcurrentProcessors and UIProgressUpdateIntervalMs are removed; AddKillaCoreFileUploadClient returns IHttpClientBuilder. See the README for upgrade notes.",
